{"name":"Crab Bisque","hex":"#f0b599","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crab","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any crustacean of the infraorder Brachyura, having five pairs of legs, the foremost of which are in the form of claws, and a carapace.","The meat of this crustacean, served as food; crabmeat."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for crabs.","To ruin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crab"},{"term":"bisque","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick creamy soup made from fish, shellfish, meat or vegetables.","A pale pinkish brown colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale pinkish brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bisque"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bisque (food)","blocks":[{"text":"Bisque or bisk is a smooth, creamy, highly seasoned soup of French origin, classically based on a strained broth (coulis) of crustaceans. It can be made from lobster, langoustine, crab, shrimp, or crayfish. The French bisque is one of the most popular seafood soups around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Lobster_bisque.jpg/330px-Lobster_bisque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bisque_(food)"},{"title":"Crab","blocks":[{"text":"Crabs are decapod crustaceans, either the Brachyura or various groups within the closely related Anomura, characterised by having a heavily armoured shell, their tail segments concealed under the body, the ability to run sideways, and the habit of hiding in rocky crevices. They do not form a single natural group or clade, but have convergently evolved multiple times from the ancestral decapod body plan through carcinisation, the process of creating this set of characteristics. As a group, they are thus polyphyletic, meaning they have multiple evolutionary origins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Cancer_pagurus.jpg/330px-Cancer_pagurus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crab"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg/1280px-Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Horseshoe_crab_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorseshoe_crab_(white_background).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Liocarcinus_vernalis.jpg/500px-Liocarcinus_vernalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Liocarcinus_vernalis.jpg/1280px-Liocarcinus_vernalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Liocarcinus_vernalis.jpg/500px-Liocarcinus_vernalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiocarcinus_vernalis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/PeerJ_-_Allopetrolisthes_punctatus.jpg/500px-PeerJ_-_Allopetrolisthes_punctatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/PeerJ_-_Allopetrolisthes_punctatus.jpg/500px-PeerJ_-_Allopetrolisthes_punctatus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.